/// A Google Font the merchant has added to this store's font library.
///
/// The library exists so a typeface is pasted ONCE and stays selectable
/// forever. Before this model, the storefront font was a free-text Google
/// Fonts embed pasted into UI -> Site Setting on every single change: nothing
/// was remembered, so returning to a font used last month meant going back to
/// fonts.google.com and fetching the snippet again. Rows here are what the
/// storefront and admin-panel font pickers list.
///
/// `url` is ALWAYS a value returned by parseGoogleFontEmbed (see
/// src/app/module/store-setting/google-font.ts) — rebuilt from validated
/// components, with `display=swap` forced, and never a substring of what the
/// merchant pasted. That parser is the security boundary for this model and is
/// reused unmodified; do not add a second path that writes this column from
/// raw input, and do not relax it to accept a non-Google host. The host check
/// is an equality test on purpose: `endsWith` would accept
/// `fonts.googleapis.com.evil.test`.
///
/// Because the parser accepts a bare URL as a paste form, a stored `url`
/// re-parses to itself. That idempotence is what lets a row be re-validated on
/// edit through exactly the same code path as a fresh paste.
///
/// The SELECTION is not stored here. StoreSetting.theme holds `font` and
/// `adminFont` as denormalised `{ family, url }` copies rather than a foreign
/// key, so the storefront read path (resolveFontStack / resolveFontHref /
/// layout.tsx) is untouched by this model existing, and so a stale selection
/// still renders a real typeface instead of nothing. The costs of that choice
/// are paid in font.service.ts: editing a row propagates to any surface
/// selected on it, and deleting a row that is selected is refused with 409.
/// See openspec/changes/add-font-library-and-admin-font, design.md Decisions
/// 1, 2, 4 and 5.
model Font {
  id String @id @default(cuid())

  /// Human-readable and with spaces — "Open Sans", never "Open+Sans". The
  /// parser decodes the `+` Google uses in the query string, and this is the
  /// value rendered in the picker and written into `--font-sans`.
  ///
  /// Unique because two library entries for one typeface would show the same
  /// card twice in the picker. The service rejects duplicates
  /// case-insensitively before insert; this constraint is the backstop that
  /// makes the check non-racy rather than the primary gate.
  family String @unique

  /// The rebuilt fonts.googleapis.com stylesheet URL. Not unique: two families
  /// never share one, but two rows differing only in requested weights would,
  /// and that is a legitimate edit rather than a duplicate.
  url String

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([family])
}
